confirmed.evidence:
Reproduced with real code. HEAD is 63fbc2d, but its only changes since a6b0b23 are in docs/ and e2e/, so the source is the same. I wrote a throwaway test, tests/server/zz_verify_checks_status.test.ts (untracked, deleted afterwards, git status clean). It builds a real CheckRunner with a fake queryImpl held behind a gate and debounceMs=10, and passes that runner to buildApp({checks: runner}), so app.ts:112-118 wires bus.on('deck.changed') -> scheduleAfterAccept. The test then emits {type:'deck.changed'} on app.bus, which is what LaneService.accept emits at laneService.ts:60, and waits until the first check query is in flight.

Command: npx vitest run tests/server/zz_verify_checks_status.test.ts --testTimeout=60000
Output:
  runner checks.status event: {"type":"checks.status","running":["arc"]}
  GET /api/checks/status during scheduled run: {"running":[],"lastRun":{"arc":null,"order":null,"gaps":null,"render":null}}
  POST /api/checks/run during scheduled run: 202 {"started":["arc","order","gaps","render"]}

Cause: routes/checks.ts:30-31 keeps its own `running` Set and `lastRun` map. These change only inside the POST handler (lines 44-54). CheckRunner keeps a separate `running` array (runner.ts:104, setRunning at line 212). Runs from scheduleAfterAccept, trigger (run_check tool) and scheduleAfterLane never reach the route's state. So the dedupe at checks.ts:44 cannot see them, and the POST calls runner.run 4 more times. enqueue (runner.ts:162) queues those 4 behind the scheduled ones instead of merging them, which gives 8 queries instead of 4. That count comes from reading the code, not the run. I did not confirm the final count: the render check renders real thumbnails and did not finish within the 30 s wait.
